<title>ISRAEL: Israel's Elco Q1 net down.</title>
<headline>Israel's Elco Q1 net down.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-05-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Elco Holdings Ltd reported the following results.</p>
<p>			 (in thousands of shekels except per share)</p>
<p>			     Q1 97	Q1 96</p>
<p>Sales			711,537    895,179</p>
<p>Operating income	  18,898     44,328</p>
<p>Other income		 8,864     31,254</p>
<p>Pretax income	     25,073     65,963</p>
<p>Net income		   9,365     23,775</p>
<p>Earnings per share	 1.25	 3.17</p>
<p>The decline in sales is the result of lower sales at its subsidiaries Electra Consumer Products (78 percent owned) and Shekem Ltd (44 percent owned), said Elco managing director Uri Kviatek.</p>
<p>The decline in Shekem's sales was mainly due to the recent sale of its supermarket chain.</p>
<p>($1=3.40 shekels)</p>
<p>-Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
</text>
